  <text xml:lang="ta" type="edition">
    <body>

        <div xml:id="AN235.1-kilavi">
          <p type="edition">talaimakaṉ piriviṉkaṇ talaimaka ḷāṟṟāmai mītūrat tōḻikkuc colliyatu.</p>
          <p type="translation" xml:lang="en">What SHE said to the confidante during the separation from HIM when [her] lack of strength became pressing. </p>
        </div>
        <div rend="parallel">
      <lg xml:id="AN235.1">
        <l>amma vāḻi tōḻi poruḷpurin</l>
        <l>tuḷḷār kollō kātala ruḷḷiyuñ</l>
        <l>ciṟanta ceytiyiṉ maṟantaṉar<anchor n="1"/> kollō</l>
        <l>payaṉilaṅ kuḻaiya vīcip peyaṉmuṉintu</l>
        <l>viṇṭu muṉṉiya koṇṭaṉ māmaḻai</l>
        <l>maṅku laṟkamoṭu poṅkupu tuḷippa</l>
        <l>vāṭaiyoṭu nivanta vāyitaḻt tōṉṟi</l>
        <l>cuṭarko ḷakaliṟ curuṅkupiṇi yaviḻac</l>
        <l>curimukiḻ mucuṇṭaip potiyaviḻ vāṉpū</l>
        <l>vicumpaṇi mīṉiṟ pacumputa la<supplied>ṇi</supplied>yak</l>
        <l>kaḷvaṉ maṇṇaḷaic ceṟiya vakalvayiṟ</l>
        <l>kiḷaiviri karumpiṉ kaṇaikkāl vāṉpū</l>
        <l>māriyaṅ kuru<supplied>ki ṉī</supplied>riya kuraṅka</l>
        <l>naṉikaṭuñ civappoṭu nāman tōṉṟip</l>
        <l>paṉikaṭi koṇṭa paṇpil vāṭai</l>
        <l>maruḷi mālaiyō ṭaruḷiṉṟu naliya</l>
        <l>nutaliṟai koṇṭa vayalaṟi pacalaiyoṭu</l>
        <l>toṉṉalañ citaiyac cāay</l>
        <l>yeṉṉaḷko laḷiya ḷeṉṉā tō<supplied>rē</supplied>.</l>
      </lg>
      <lg type="translation" xml:lang="en">
        <l corresp="1">Alas, oh friend, making/desiring wealth,</l>
        <l corresp="2">does he remember, our lover? And even if he remembers,</l>
        <l corresp="3">did he forget [us] over exalted acts [to be done],</l>
        <l corresp="4">while, gushing forth so that the fertile ground is muddy, raining with a vengeance,</l>
        <l corresp="5">from the clouds that approached the sky, great rain</l>
        <l corresp="6">foams [and] drizzles, along with the remainder of the clouds</l>
        <l corresp="7">while Malabar lilies with choice petals that have come up with the north wind</l>
        <l corresp="8">open [their] shrunken outer petals like glowing clay lamps,</l>
        <l corresp="9">while the white flowers that open in bundles on the bindweed budding in curls</l>
        <l corresp="10">adorn the green bushes like stars adorn the sky,</l>
        <l corresp="11">while the robber keeps to [his] earthen cave, while on the vast side</l>
        <l corresp="12">the white flowers on the round stalks of the branching sugarcane</l>
        <l corresp="13">dangle wet like pretty ibises in a shower,</l>
        <l corresp="14">while, as fear appears with very fierce anger,</l>
        <l corresp="15">the virtueless north wind that has taken over the protection of the dew</l>
        <l corresp="16">confusingly afflicts [us] without mercy, along with the evening,</l>
        <l corresp="19cd">– he who does not say,</l>
        <l corresp="17">“with pallor, known to the neighbourhood, that settles on [her] forehead,</l>
        <l corresp="18">emaciated so that [her] old beauty is spoiled</l>
        <l corresp="19ab" rend="indent4">how will she be, pitiable she?”</l>
      </lg>
        </div>
    </body>
  </text>

